nges sign, and\n\n- the tangent line to the graph exists.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our graph.\n\n- The point $x=1$ is a point of inflection. Indeed: \n\n- the graph changes concavity from concave down to concave up at $x=1,$ and\n\n- the tangent line exists at this point.\n\n- The point $x=3$ is *not* a point of inflection for two reasons. First, the function does not change concavity. It's concave up both to the left and to the right of $x=3.$ Second, the tangent line does not exist at this point.\n\n- The point $x=5$ is *not* a point of inflection for two reasons. First, the function does not change concavity. It's concave up both to the left and to the right of $x=5.$ Second, the function is not defined at this point, so the tangent line does not exist either.\n\nTherefore, the point of inflection is $x=1$ only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033744/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b4b197424b83a96f51c510aee83ade4007f9068e9bd11ea0df23ab2a04da19"} {"question" "q-51428" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033744/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6a63de4c5e2bc9e8346c877ebf97d88a81300f9bef1d35d05a6cc202be70fd30"} {"question" "q-51428" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033744/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6b4b197424b83a96f51c510aee83ade4007f9068e9bd11ea0df23ab2a04da19"} {"question" "q-51428" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$x=1$ and $x=3$"] ["text" "$x=1$ and $x=5$"] ["text" "$x=1$ only"] ["text" "$x=3$ and $x=5$"] ["text" "$x=3$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/